==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|spýja}} (compare {{cog|fo|spýggja}}, {{etyl|no|-}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} and {{etyl|da|-}} {{m|sv|spy}}), from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*spīwaną}}, whence also {{cog|nl|spuwen}}, {{cog|de|speien}}, {{cog|en|spew}}, {{cog|got|𐍃𐍀𐌴𐌹𐍅𐌰𐌽}}. Ultimately from {{der|is|ine-pro|*(s)ptyēw-||to spit, vomit}}. Non-Germanic cognates include {{cog|xcl|թուք}}, {{cog|fa|تف||spittle}}, {{cog|os|ту||spittle}}, {{cog|grc|πτύω||I spit out}}, {{cog|la|spuo}}, {{cog|cu|пльвати}} ({{cog|ru|плевать}}) and {{cog|sa|ष्ठीवति||to spit}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈspiːja/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|iːja}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|spjó|spjóu|spúið}} ''or'' {{is-verb-weak|spúði|spúið}}

# to [[vomit]]
# to [[spit]] out, make [[gush]] forth

====Conjugation====
Strong or (increasingly commonly) weak. May also be mixed, with the strong forms being retained mostly in the singular past indicative forms.

===Noun===
{{is-noun|f|spýju|spýjur}}

# [[vomit]]
# a thick [[shower]] of [[rain]] in windy conditions
# a small [[avalanche]]

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-f-w1|sp|ý|j}}

